WEBVTT

00:50.175 --> 00:52.969
ALL CHARACTERS, LOCATIONS,
ORGANIZATIONS, RELIGIONS,

00:53.052 --> 00:55.889
EVENTS, AND OCCUPATIONS
IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

01:30.215 --> 01:32.217
JUNG YI-HYUN,
THE PRIDE OF SEYANG HIGH SCHOOL

01:32.300 --> 01:33.510
HIS KNEE IS BUSTED!

01:33.593 --> 01:35.303
HE'S DOOMED!

01:44.479 --> 01:45.313
The megaphone.

01:47.565 --> 01:48.775
Jung Yi-hyun!

01:48.858 --> 01:51.611
I know how you feel.
I was in Little League too.

01:52.112 --> 01:55.365
So come down and talk. Come down.

01:55.448 --> 01:57.158
You can just talk from there.

01:57.784 --> 02:00.036
- What did he say?
- I couldn't hear him.

02:00.120 --> 02:02.038
Then give him a megaphone too.

02:03.289 --> 02:06.417
I'll go up there, so wait a bit.

02:06.501 --> 02:08.795
Let's talk when I get up there.

02:08.878 --> 02:10.213
Where are the stairs?

02:17.178 --> 02:18.388
He's just not coming down.

02:19.097 --> 02:20.932
Focus on your books.

02:22.142 --> 02:25.353
If you focus, you can't even hear
a bomb exploding next to you.

02:25.436 --> 02:27.605
But classes are over.
Why aren't we going home?

02:27.689 --> 02:29.232
No one can focus right now anyway.

02:29.315 --> 02:32.443
Do you think Yi-hyun would be
happy if you ran out in a crowd?

02:33.111 --> 02:34.904
He's already mentally unstable.

02:34.988 --> 02:37.490
And if he jumps off impulsively
after seeing you guys,

02:38.116 --> 02:41.411
I'm sure that'll help you focus
when you get home.

02:42.078 --> 02:44.330
So you'll send us home
if he comes down, right?

02:44.414 --> 02:47.167
Yes, I'll send you home right away.

02:47.250 --> 02:48.918
The police are negotiating with him,

02:49.002 --> 02:51.421
so don’t provoke me.
Just lie on your desk and sleep.

02:52.672 --> 02:54.424
You've been a student for a long time.

02:54.507 --> 02:55.925
It must be hard for you too.

02:56.509 --> 02:59.429
- I'm going to the restroom.
- Hey, I told you not to provoke me…

03:01.681 --> 03:03.516
Well, let's just keep quiet, please.

03:03.600 --> 03:04.851
Hey, all of you, focus!

03:04.934 --> 03:07.103
Focus on your books.
The bomb is being dropped.

03:09.606 --> 03:14.944
I will make sure
that you're all cured, okay?

03:15.028 --> 03:17.906
If that can't be done,
I'll make you a cop at the very least.

03:17.989 --> 03:20.116
So trust me and come down, okay?

03:20.700 --> 03:21.868
I don't want to be a cop.

03:21.951 --> 03:23.202
All right!

03:26.873 --> 03:30.084
I'm his friend. I was told to come up
so I can help negotiate with him.

03:30.168 --> 03:33.379
Talk here. I won't go. Talk here, okay?

03:33.880 --> 03:35.423
Calm down first.

03:36.799 --> 03:37.842
Yoon Sae-bom?

03:38.635 --> 03:39.761
Hey!

03:40.595 --> 03:41.846
Hey!

03:42.555 --> 03:44.891
Hey, young lady!

03:44.974 --> 03:46.434
Wait!

03:46.517 --> 03:47.602
Who are you?

03:48.102 --> 03:50.230
- Are you his girlfriend?
- No.

03:50.313 --> 03:52.190
Hey, we can't go home because of you!

03:52.815 --> 03:55.568
Mister, I will persuade him,
so wait there for a moment.

03:56.069 --> 03:58.363
What's wrong with
the students at this school?

04:04.160 --> 04:05.912
Are you upset you can't play baseball?

04:06.412 --> 04:07.789
That's not what it is.

04:08.748 --> 04:10.750
I just came up here
because I was frustrated,

04:10.833 --> 04:13.419
but ambulances and police cars
suddenly arrived.

04:14.587 --> 04:16.214
Which idiot made a report?

04:17.507 --> 04:19.884
I'm just waiting to see
how far this will go.

04:19.968 --> 04:21.261
I have nothing to do anyway.

04:22.053 --> 04:24.138
Don't you have anything to do
besides baseball?

04:24.222 --> 04:25.056
I don't.

04:25.682 --> 04:27.183
I did it my entire life.

04:27.267 --> 04:28.768
I was really good at it too.

04:29.269 --> 04:31.896
And I ended up like this.
Would you be okay if you were me?

04:31.980 --> 04:34.232
I did nothing my entire life,
but I was okay.

04:34.315 --> 04:36.693
Hey, doing nothing is way better.

04:37.193 --> 04:38.861
I was hospitalized for a long time.

04:38.945 --> 04:41.489
And you know, it all just becomes
a good memory later on.

04:42.532 --> 04:44.826
I can't play baseball ever again.

04:44.909 --> 04:48.288
My life is over.
I don't know what to do in my life.

04:52.792 --> 04:53.876
What about you, then?

04:53.960 --> 04:55.545
What are you going to do?

04:56.671 --> 04:58.506
I wanted to be a nurse until last week,

04:58.589 --> 05:00.300
but a public official seems nice too.

05:00.383 --> 05:02.844
I would need a monthly paycheck,

05:02.927 --> 05:04.220
but I keep changing my mind.

05:04.721 --> 05:07.974
See? You're feeling unsettled too
for being two years behind.

05:08.057 --> 05:09.267
No.

05:10.226 --> 05:13.563
I'm saying there's no limit
to our futures.

05:15.732 --> 05:18.985
It's okay, so just do it,

05:19.068 --> 05:21.279
and think that it's fine
even if it doesn't work.

05:38.504 --> 05:39.714
Like me.

06:19.629 --> 06:20.797
No, Mister.

06:20.880 --> 06:24.550
I planned to make him fall
onto the cushion.

06:45.488 --> 06:47.156
Okay, let's talk when we get there.

06:47.949 --> 06:49.283
- Let go of me!
- Hey!

06:49.951 --> 06:51.077
Jung Yi-hyun!

06:51.160 --> 06:54.038
Tell him that you don't want me
to get punished.

06:54.122 --> 06:55.623
He's going to arrest me.

06:55.706 --> 06:56.999
Hey, Yoon Sae-bom.

07:03.256 --> 07:04.757
Do you want to be my girlfriend?

07:24.068 --> 07:26.237
12 YEARS LATER

07:29.699 --> 07:31.534
SPECIAL OPERATION UNIT

07:59.812 --> 08:00.855
Salute!

08:09.197 --> 08:10.698
What are you doing? Treat him!

08:17.830 --> 08:18.956
What are his injuries?

08:19.040 --> 08:20.583
He got shot in the chest,

08:21.083 --> 08:22.293
and he can't breathe.

08:29.550 --> 08:30.843
It's a pneumothorax.

08:30.927 --> 08:32.970
The air's leaking
from the hole in his lung

08:33.054 --> 08:35.765
- and creating pressure--
- Don’t explain. Treat him!

08:40.937 --> 08:42.772
TRAINEE LEE JONG-TAE

08:44.065 --> 08:45.858
Do I really do it?

08:45.942 --> 08:47.818
Don't think. Just do as you learned.

08:56.994 --> 08:59.539
Instructor!

09:07.880 --> 09:10.466
You're going to break my ribs, you jerk.

09:12.927 --> 09:13.761
Instructor.

09:27.024 --> 09:29.026
That was my clavicle, you idiot.

09:32.780 --> 09:36.492
Trainee Lee Jong-tae,
you just killed your teammate.

09:37.034 --> 09:38.869
You get a deduction on your TMP course.

09:38.953 --> 09:40.913
TMP: A TACTICAL FIRST AID TRAINING COURSE

09:42.415 --> 09:43.791
TEST SCORE
TMP COURSE

09:53.134 --> 09:55.678
Your acting was great today.

09:55.761 --> 09:57.388
- Did I do great?
- Yes.

10:00.891 --> 10:03.978
Wear your gloves, or you'll slip.

10:04.061 --> 10:05.313
Bye.

10:06.063 --> 10:07.607
Are you really deducting points?

10:07.690 --> 10:10.359
Yes, he's slow in making judgments,
and he's cowardly.

10:11.485 --> 10:15.156
Based on your standards,
everyone in the world is slow, Sae-bom.

10:15.656 --> 10:17.158
SPECIAL OPERATION UNIT
TRAINEE YOON SAE-BOM

10:26.208 --> 10:28.085
- Salute!
- Salute!

10:33.841 --> 10:36.927
When someone gets shot and can't breathe,

10:37.011 --> 10:38.220
what are you supposed to--

10:39.138 --> 10:39.972
What the…

10:42.558 --> 10:43.893
Hey, don't do that!

10:44.435 --> 10:45.895
Yoon Sae-bom!

10:46.687 --> 10:47.897
What are you doing?

10:49.065 --> 10:51.525
They had to make this because of you.

10:51.609 --> 10:54.362
You stabbed his chest directly with it

10:55.321 --> 10:58.199
and had Team Chief Choi
demoted to a patrol division.

10:58.699 --> 11:02.286
He called me recently
and said it's the perfect place for him.

11:02.370 --> 11:03.287
Really?

11:03.913 --> 11:05.623
He sent me a gift coupon.

11:06.248 --> 11:07.583
Then what about me?

11:08.292 --> 11:10.127
Why didn't he send me one?

11:10.211 --> 11:11.962
I'm sure he had a reason.

11:12.046 --> 11:13.923
I'm hungry.

11:14.006 --> 11:15.299
Let's go eat.

11:18.427 --> 11:22.306
MOTEL

11:37.530 --> 11:38.948
Hello, this is the front desk.

11:39.657 --> 11:41.075
Yes, I can hear it too.

11:41.784 --> 11:42.952
The second floor?

11:43.994 --> 11:45.496
Okay, I'll go talk to them.

11:47.957 --> 11:51.419
What are they doing
at this early hour? Seriously…

12:03.305 --> 12:07.643
Excuse me, you have to pay
if you damage the motel's property.

12:15.568 --> 12:16.902
Do you want to get beaten up?

12:29.999 --> 12:33.002
It's hard to endure weather
that's gradually getting hotter,

12:33.085 --> 12:38.048
but we're happy for being able
to breathe without wearing masks now.

12:38.132 --> 12:41.260
The world has changed a bit
from before the COVID-19 pandemic,

12:41.343 --> 12:45.264
but thanks to that, we learned
how precious normal daily lives are.

12:45.347 --> 12:49.560
Dear listeners, I hope you can smile
looking at each other's uncovered faces,

12:49.643 --> 12:52.605
take a deep breath
upon looking at the blue sky,

12:52.688 --> 12:55.608
and have a great afternoon.

12:55.691 --> 12:58.819
Dear listeners, have a great day,

12:58.903 --> 13:00.613
and tomorrow…

13:01.989 --> 13:04.074
COVID-19 MAY BE OVER BUT WE DON'T KNOW
WHEN ANOTHER DISEASE MAY BREAK OUT AGAIN

13:07.661 --> 13:13.542
JUNG YI-HYUN

13:15.503 --> 13:16.545
Here.

13:16.629 --> 13:19.340
Hey, do you still want to play
baseball even with that knee?

13:19.423 --> 13:21.717
I get paid to play for this team.

13:21.800 --> 13:23.886
- What kind of a case is it?
- Murder.

13:23.969 --> 13:25.971
You didn't even know what the case was?

13:26.055 --> 13:28.098
I was told to come, so I came.

13:28.182 --> 13:30.059
I even gave up my day off and my game.

13:30.142 --> 13:32.520
- You should thank me.
- Oh, thank you so much.

13:33.229 --> 13:34.980
People from the next room reported it.

13:35.064 --> 13:36.732
- I heard the scream and--
- Excuse me.

13:36.815 --> 13:39.276
- Who's the victim?
- The front desk employee.

13:39.360 --> 13:40.194
Let's go.

13:40.277 --> 13:42.905
- All I need to do is testify?
- I can't believe this.

14:10.891 --> 14:13.227
What did they do to his neck?

14:15.020 --> 14:16.438
Well, that looks like

14:17.147 --> 14:19.191
it was done with a dull blade, right?

14:19.275 --> 14:20.818
Perhaps they wanted him to suffer.

14:20.901 --> 14:23.696
- Who's the suspect?
- The guest who stayed here.

14:23.779 --> 14:26.240
There were a lot of complaints
because he was so noisy.

14:27.074 --> 14:28.909
But who covered him with this?

14:34.039 --> 14:37.084
- Did you meddle with the crime scene?
- No, we didn't touch anything.

14:37.167 --> 14:39.378
- Any witnesses?
- None so far.

14:40.671 --> 14:42.506
He said it was like this from the start.

14:45.050 --> 14:46.802
Did they check the security cams?

14:46.886 --> 14:48.387
Right. The security cams.

14:53.058 --> 14:54.852
Hey, what about the security cams?

14:56.103 --> 15:00.190
They're checking it now,
but they can't find the suspect leaving.

15:02.151 --> 15:04.737
He covered the victim's face and ran away.

15:06.906 --> 15:08.741
But the camera didn't catch him leaving.

15:08.824 --> 15:12.036
I'm sure he did
an electronic access register,

15:12.119 --> 15:13.829
but the CDSCHQ won't let us see it.

15:13.913 --> 15:16.206
It's a breach
of personal information protection.

15:16.290 --> 15:17.875
Hey, killers have no rights.

15:17.958 --> 15:21.003
They should integrate
the information and arrest all of them.

15:21.086 --> 15:22.838
I don't understand.

15:26.800 --> 15:28.260
Oh, I didn't mean you.

15:28.344 --> 15:29.470
Okay.

15:34.725 --> 15:36.685
I'm sure they didn't
search in there, right?

15:50.491 --> 15:54.328
Hey, I know you investigate recklessly,
hoping for good luck, but--

15:54.411 --> 15:56.997
It can't even go near the "reckless" part.

15:57.539 --> 16:01.293
I know someone who's even more…

16:03.504 --> 16:04.505
Sir…

16:05.839 --> 16:07.091
come out.

16:07.174 --> 16:08.175
Are you kidding me?

16:09.635 --> 16:12.012
If this is another joke,
I'm going to kill you today.

16:16.141 --> 16:17.267
Damn it!

16:17.351 --> 16:18.936
Our eyes just met.

16:20.354 --> 16:22.856
Hey, we got the culprit. Don't come in.

16:22.940 --> 16:24.984
Come in later.

16:32.950 --> 16:35.160
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD, SUNG WOO-JAE

16:35.244 --> 16:37.496
Did you do this, Mr. Sung Woo-jae?

16:38.664 --> 16:39.707
I don't know.

16:41.625 --> 16:44.461
Did you cover the body
because you were scared to see the body?

16:45.045 --> 16:46.797
Then why did you kill him?

16:46.880 --> 16:48.298
You don't remember that either?

16:51.593 --> 16:53.512
I had a dream, but…

16:55.014 --> 16:56.765
Was the dream about killing him?

16:59.893 --> 17:02.771
You’re covered in blood,
so you couldn't run away.

17:03.272 --> 17:07.067
You were panicking, but the police came,
so you must've hidden.

17:07.568 --> 17:09.194
By the way, where's the weapon?

17:11.113 --> 17:12.573
What did you kill him with in the dream?

17:12.656 --> 17:14.616
Oh, that's right.

17:15.117 --> 17:17.369
The court won't acknowledge it
if there's no weapon.

17:20.748 --> 17:22.249
You see,

17:22.332 --> 17:25.210
I was thirsty for some reason, so…

17:37.264 --> 17:38.682
Did you bite him?

17:47.691 --> 17:49.026
Give me one more.

17:52.946 --> 17:54.281
ONE MAIN SIDE DISH PER PERSON

18:05.459 --> 18:07.920
Were you doing physical labor or what?

18:08.462 --> 18:10.005
Why are you eating so much?

18:10.506 --> 18:12.925
I'm upset, so don't say anything.

18:15.636 --> 18:16.637
Here.

18:18.764 --> 18:20.682
If you have something to say, go ahead.

18:28.982 --> 18:30.442
SEYANG FOREST LE CIEL
PUBLIC RENTAL APARTMENT NOTICE FOR POLICE

18:31.360 --> 18:32.444
What are you reading?

18:32.528 --> 18:35.739
They're developing
the National Police Agency's old location.

18:35.823 --> 18:37.116
They're building apartments.

18:37.908 --> 18:41.036
Three police officers' households
will get special provisions for that.

18:41.120 --> 18:43.122
Really? What are the conditions?

18:43.205 --> 18:45.749
My wife's dream is to move
into that new apartment.

18:45.833 --> 18:48.001
They give extra points
for long-term service,

18:48.085 --> 18:50.087
family members to provide for,
and newlyweds.

18:50.170 --> 18:53.715
The biggest chunks come from
arrest records and work evaluations.

18:53.799 --> 18:55.968
Once I'm chosen,
I'll get an apartment for sure.

18:56.051 --> 18:57.761
It's like winning the lottery.

18:57.845 --> 19:00.639
Who are we going to arrest? Terrorists?

19:01.807 --> 19:04.309
You never know
what might happen in life, okay?

19:04.393 --> 19:06.979
If I show something today…

19:07.479 --> 19:08.856
What are you going to show?

19:09.606 --> 19:10.774
I'm thinking.

19:22.327 --> 19:24.997
Take it easy with sports.
Don't get injured again.

19:25.080 --> 19:26.165
Okay.

19:33.088 --> 19:34.590
(I AM) THE LIFESAVER

19:35.215 --> 19:37.801
Sae-bom, are you religious now?

19:38.510 --> 19:39.428
It's my friend.

19:42.222 --> 19:43.724
The timing isn't very…

19:46.143 --> 19:47.102
Hey, what is it?

19:47.186 --> 19:50.063
Your unit was mentioned
during an investigation, so…

19:50.147 --> 19:50.981
Why?

19:51.481 --> 19:53.567
You're instructing
a training course, right?

19:53.650 --> 19:55.611
He said he got drugs from an SOU trainee.

20:03.744 --> 20:06.330
He said the drug was perfectly legal.

20:07.122 --> 20:09.499
I'm sure he just meant
you wouldn't get caught.

20:11.251 --> 20:12.711
Do you have any leftover drugs?

20:12.794 --> 20:16.882
I received three or four tablets,
but I think I took them all.

20:17.382 --> 20:19.676
- What's the name of the trainee?
- Lee Jong-tae.

20:20.469 --> 20:22.137
Lee Jong-tae?

20:22.930 --> 20:23.889
Salute!

20:23.972 --> 20:25.474
TRAINEE LEE JONG-TAE

20:26.600 --> 20:29.811
Anyway, we're sending the document.
I thought you should know.

20:30.437 --> 20:31.939
Well done.

20:32.022 --> 20:35.317
If I find the entire gang,
then I'll get an arrest record.

20:35.400 --> 20:36.693
What are you talking about?

20:36.777 --> 20:38.487
I'm just letting you know.

20:50.123 --> 20:53.835
I'll be back soon,
so keep an eye on my food.

20:54.670 --> 20:56.380
It's more important than food?

21:03.887 --> 21:05.347
That's strange.

21:18.443 --> 21:20.153
Don’t worry. I warned everyone

21:20.237 --> 21:22.447
that they're dead
if they eat your pork cutlet.

21:24.074 --> 21:25.158
What are they doing?

21:25.242 --> 21:27.995
Are they actually having sex here?

21:28.078 --> 21:29.538
Those punks…

21:31.206 --> 21:32.916
Trainee Lee Jong-tae.

21:36.628 --> 21:38.088
Trainee Lee Jong-tae!

21:38.672 --> 21:40.299
Help!

21:51.560 --> 21:52.602
What is that?

21:54.646 --> 21:56.398
Lee Jong-tae, stop right there!

22:16.501 --> 22:18.128
Seung-young, take him and go.

22:46.198 --> 22:47.699
Next, it'll be your pelvis.

22:56.041 --> 22:56.917
What is that?

22:57.751 --> 22:59.294
How should I know?

23:14.017 --> 23:15.435
I'll stay here,

23:15.936 --> 23:17.854
so you take him and get him treated.

23:22.192 --> 23:24.569
We have an emergency patient!
Anyone there?

23:24.653 --> 23:26.404
This is not a drill!

23:39.876 --> 23:44.214
Instructor, please call an ambulance.

23:44.297 --> 23:45.549
Instructor!

23:50.679 --> 23:51.847
Instructor…

24:00.272 --> 24:02.399
Instructor…

24:15.120 --> 24:16.621
Get the medical trolley.

24:23.211 --> 24:24.880
Be careful not to get bitten.

24:35.473 --> 24:36.474
(I AM) THE LIFESAVER

24:51.323 --> 24:52.157
Hey.

24:52.240 --> 24:54.951
You should've told me it was dangerous!
I almost got killed!

24:55.035 --> 24:57.078
What are you saying?
Why would you get killed?

24:57.662 --> 24:59.998
How could he not feel pain
even when he got shot?

25:00.081 --> 25:01.917
Who shot who? Hey, are you okay?

25:02.792 --> 25:05.128
I'm okay, of course, but…

25:05.212 --> 25:07.547
How could you catch someone
like that without a gun?

25:08.548 --> 25:10.425
I just persuaded him by talking to him.

25:10.926 --> 25:13.428
How is that possible?
You could get through to him?

25:14.054 --> 25:16.014
Hey, tell me what happened in detail.

25:16.097 --> 25:17.432
Did you meet Lee Jong-tae?

25:17.515 --> 25:18.475
Yes.

25:19.392 --> 25:22.646
Did he… try to bite you?

25:22.729 --> 25:24.189
So you do know about it.

25:25.273 --> 25:27.192
What kind of nonsense is this…

25:28.985 --> 25:31.738
Hello? Hey, Yoon Sae-bom!

25:32.405 --> 25:33.865
Hey, are you okay?

25:34.491 --> 25:36.493
Hey, answer me! Hey!

25:36.576 --> 25:37.410
Yes?

25:38.203 --> 25:41.706
Why didn't you answer? You scared me.

26:32.549 --> 26:34.175
Corporal Yoon Sae-bom.

26:37.762 --> 26:39.264
This is the ladies' restroom.

26:39.347 --> 26:41.182
The guy you shot.

26:41.266 --> 26:43.310
There's a possibility
he has an infectious disease.

26:53.695 --> 26:55.530
What infectious disease?

26:55.613 --> 26:57.449
We're currently investigating.

26:57.532 --> 27:00.201
Sae-bom, who are you talking to right now?

27:04.039 --> 27:07.667
Lieutenant Colonel Han Tae-seok from
the Crisis Management Center at CDSCHQ.

27:08.501 --> 27:10.253
Corporal Yoon will call you back.

27:12.047 --> 27:15.550
Give me your gun and cooperate
with the disease investigation.

27:42.160 --> 27:43.328
Who are you people?

27:43.411 --> 27:45.413
- You can eat my pork cutlet.
- Sae-bom.

27:45.497 --> 27:48.083
The National Police Agency
will send guidelines soon.

27:48.166 --> 27:49.959
What happened earlier was an accident.

27:50.043 --> 27:51.044
So keep this secret.

27:51.127 --> 27:54.089
Corporal Yoon has the risk
of infection, so we're taking her.

27:57.092 --> 27:59.469
(I AM) THE LIFESAVER

28:01.721 --> 28:03.932
- Hello?
- Lieutenant Colonel Han Tae-seok?

28:04.682 --> 28:06.017
Wait, please don't hang up.

28:06.101 --> 28:08.770
I'm Corporal Jung Yi-hyun
from Seyang Police Station.

28:08.853 --> 28:11.564
Can you please briefly explain
what's going on?

28:11.648 --> 28:15.652
Corporal Yoon has been in contact with
an infected trainee so she must be tested.

28:18.196 --> 28:19.864
Does that mean she's okay now?

28:20.657 --> 28:23.243
She's essential personnel,
so she's fully vaccinated too.

28:23.326 --> 28:25.870
What infection are you talking about?

28:25.954 --> 28:27.997
We'll have to find out. I'll hang up now.

28:28.081 --> 28:30.959
It's Lee Jong-tae, right?
The infected trainee.

28:31.626 --> 28:33.670
We also arrested a murder suspect

28:33.753 --> 28:36.005
who was in contact with Lee Jong-tae.

28:36.089 --> 28:37.465
Did you say murder?

28:37.549 --> 28:39.676
He bit someone's neck.

28:40.218 --> 28:42.512
Is that symptom related to the infection?

28:43.805 --> 28:46.057
Did you say Seyang Station? I'll be there.

28:46.141 --> 28:47.434
Wait.

28:47.517 --> 28:50.270
Should all those who were
in contact be in quarantine too?

28:50.353 --> 28:52.731
If they were bitten or scratched, yes.

29:01.573 --> 29:04.200
SEYANG POLICE STATION

29:11.166 --> 29:13.793
As long as you weren't bitten
or scratched, you're fine.

29:15.044 --> 29:16.463
You're Mr. Han Tae-seok, right?

29:17.005 --> 29:18.423
Where's Sae-bom?

29:20.759 --> 29:22.886
She's being tested in a safe place.

29:25.930 --> 29:31.686
THE 3RD WONJUNG UNIVERSITY
ANTI-REDEVELOPMENT RALLY

29:37.108 --> 29:39.903
WONJUNG UNIVERSITY
DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING

29:46.951 --> 29:48.536
STOP

30:07.388 --> 30:08.431
LIEUTENANT COLONEL HAN TAE-SEOK

30:09.849 --> 30:12.143
You're military,
but you're doing civilian work.

30:12.227 --> 30:15.396
It's important to show that
the two can cooperate in times of crisis.

30:16.189 --> 30:20.443
So this is an infectious disease
that makes people bite other people?

30:20.985 --> 30:24.656
We're thinking that it's
a mutant virus that affects the brain.

30:25.156 --> 30:28.701
When you're bitten, you either die
from excessive bleeding or get infected.

30:29.202 --> 30:33.081
Gosh, droplets aren't enough anymore,
now the diseases even spread from bites.

30:33.164 --> 30:35.542
The infection channels are limited,
so don't worry,

30:35.625 --> 30:38.044
and just work hard
on your assigned duties.

30:38.127 --> 30:39.921
Hang on.

30:40.004 --> 30:42.298
We don't need to be
in self-quarantine, right?

30:42.382 --> 30:44.926
You just need to write
and sign a confidentiality oath.

30:45.677 --> 30:48.304
That suspect said that he did it
after he took drugs.

30:50.306 --> 30:53.184
The drugs he received
from his SOU trainee friend.

30:55.019 --> 30:57.522
Do you have that drug?

30:58.690 --> 30:59.566
No.

31:00.066 --> 31:03.319
Maybe it's just a side effect
of a hallucinogenic, not a disease.

31:03.403 --> 31:07.615
There's no possibility of that,
but it may have had an influence.

31:07.699 --> 31:09.492
Contact me when you find the drug.

31:13.413 --> 31:14.914
Corporal Jung Yi-hyun.

31:16.666 --> 31:18.251
Are you playing baseball again?

31:18.334 --> 31:20.670
You were quite
a rising star in high school.

31:21.588 --> 31:24.591
I can't run at my full speed anymore, so…

31:26.718 --> 31:27.760
That's too bad.

31:32.223 --> 31:34.809
He must be a big baseball fan.
He recognized you.

31:34.893 --> 31:36.644
Did Sung Woo-jae get tested for narcotics?

31:36.728 --> 31:38.313
Yes, we sent his hair to KCSI.

31:38.396 --> 31:41.316
I'll give you a number,
so track it down and find where it is.

31:42.233 --> 31:44.652
- Hey, where are you going?
- To find the drug.

32:52.553 --> 32:54.931
Jung-kook, I found it.

32:55.014 --> 32:57.308
I'm calling you
so you won't waste your time.

32:57.392 --> 32:59.644
The test results just came out.

32:59.727 --> 33:00.812
It's perfectly clean.

33:02.814 --> 33:04.190
Oh, really?

33:04.273 --> 33:06.776
Yes, I guess it really is
an infectious disease.

33:06.859 --> 33:09.946
Would it be okay for me to go home today?

33:10.029 --> 33:11.948
Hey, if I show my teeth to my wife…

33:12.031 --> 33:13.950
- Wait…
- Then I'll lose all of them.

33:14.450 --> 33:15.785
Then what about what I found?

33:15.868 --> 33:17.870
Cold remedies, painkillers, vitamins…

33:17.954 --> 33:19.288
There are all kinds of drugs.

33:19.372 --> 33:22.458
Stop wasting your time. Just go home.

33:37.598 --> 33:43.938
SUPER ROOKIE BASEBALL ACADEMY

33:50.528 --> 33:51.863
Hey, Il-ho.

34:04.751 --> 34:07.170
Hey, why didn't you play
at the game today?

34:07.253 --> 34:08.546
Come inside.

34:18.222 --> 34:21.059
You should call me
or answer my calls, at least.

34:21.142 --> 34:22.935
Everyone nagged me about it.

34:23.019 --> 34:24.353
Stop nagging me.

34:25.063 --> 34:26.397
Hey, more than that…

34:27.565 --> 34:28.858
Look at this.

34:28.941 --> 34:30.234
What is this?

34:30.318 --> 34:32.487
I think it's a narcotic.
Do you know what it is?

34:32.570 --> 34:34.072
Why would you bring this to me?

34:34.155 --> 34:36.657
Don't get the wrong idea
and listen to me, okay?

34:36.741 --> 34:38.743
You got kicked out because of drugs.

34:38.826 --> 34:40.578
I only took it by mistake.

34:40.661 --> 34:42.705
You call yourself a friend?

34:42.789 --> 34:44.832
No, you were trying
to get better at baseball.

34:44.916 --> 34:47.126
I wanted to be good too,
but it didn't work out.

34:47.210 --> 34:48.961
Don't even bring up the past.

34:49.045 --> 34:50.546
Right. The past.

34:50.630 --> 34:52.882
You later made up your mind
and studied very hard.

34:52.965 --> 34:55.343
Sports medicine and computers.

34:57.929 --> 35:00.306
This is really important to me, all right?

35:04.560 --> 35:05.686
This isn't a narcotic.

35:06.437 --> 35:07.271
Why not?

35:07.814 --> 35:09.524
Do you see the serial numbers here?

35:10.691 --> 35:12.443
No one does that for narcotics.

35:12.527 --> 35:15.446
This was made by a pharmaceutical company.

35:15.530 --> 35:18.241
You'll be able to find it
in the pharmaceutical database.

35:18.324 --> 35:20.201
- Find out what it is.
- Me?

35:20.284 --> 35:22.036
- Until when?
- Now.

35:25.164 --> 35:26.499
Wake me up when you're done.

35:50.648 --> 35:52.191
Are you collecting my blood, too?

36:32.398 --> 36:34.233
What is this place?

36:35.026 --> 36:37.737
It doesn't look like a hospital.
It looks like a school.

36:37.820 --> 36:41.407
We can't set neck-biting infected free
in a place crowded with people.

36:42.491 --> 36:46.245
Am I going to become like
Trainee Lee Jong-tae, too?

36:54.795 --> 36:57.381
I was teasing. I won't bite.

36:58.049 --> 37:01.552
- You'll get hurt if you do that.
- So please answer me.

37:06.557 --> 37:08.726
I thought you were putting ointment on me.

37:15.233 --> 37:18.361
What should I do now
until the results come out?

37:19.737 --> 37:21.155
Testify.

37:22.156 --> 37:24.325
Tell me about what happened today.

37:26.869 --> 37:29.872
I saw Trainee Lee Jong-tae
attacking a fellow trainee,

37:29.956 --> 37:31.457
and tried to stop him.

37:31.540 --> 37:33.251
How did Lee Jong-tae seem?

37:33.334 --> 37:34.669
He was in a bad condition.

37:34.752 --> 37:36.462
Be more specific, please.

37:36.545 --> 37:41.133
Both of his eyes were milky,
like he had cataracts,

37:41.217 --> 37:43.719
and he tried to bite me like a beast.

37:44.512 --> 37:48.266
I shot him twice, but it seemed like
he couldn't feel any pain.

37:49.058 --> 37:53.354
Is this like some kind of rabies?

37:54.814 --> 37:55.940
It's similar.

37:56.732 --> 38:00.194
My detective friend said that
he might've been on narcotics.

38:00.278 --> 38:02.154
If someone goes mad and bites a person,

38:02.238 --> 38:04.657
the police would believe
that it was because of drugs.

38:04.740 --> 38:06.534
Because that's the easiest answer.

38:07.159 --> 38:10.288
And an infectious disease is
an easier answer for you.

38:10.371 --> 38:12.707
Because people see what they believe.

38:12.790 --> 38:13.791
But…

38:15.126 --> 38:16.627
aren't you a police officer, too?

38:18.045 --> 38:20.214
We specialize in dealing
with terrorist attacks.

38:20.298 --> 38:21.924
We only get paid by the police.

38:28.055 --> 38:29.598
Is Trainee Lee Jong-tae…

38:31.100 --> 38:32.351
okay?

38:33.019 --> 38:34.562
He's miraculously recovering.

38:35.354 --> 38:38.316
We will get you a place to rest
until the test results come out.

38:39.233 --> 38:41.610
Aren't you giving my phone back?

38:42.194 --> 38:43.904
We'll bring a telephone to your room.

38:53.289 --> 39:00.296
UNKNOWN NUMBER

39:08.054 --> 39:10.848
- Hello?
- You got me into this mess!

39:12.350 --> 39:13.476
Yoon Sae-bom?

39:14.185 --> 39:16.562
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

39:16.645 --> 39:18.939
It's cleaner than
the public official apartment.

39:19.023 --> 39:20.775
That place is over 50 years old.

39:20.858 --> 39:23.110
It always leaked
and the pipes froze in winter.

39:23.694 --> 39:25.946
And they put three people into one house!

39:26.030 --> 39:27.490
It's cold.

39:30.910 --> 39:33.537
Can they afford to pay
the electricity bills?

39:33.621 --> 39:35.915
How's your condition? Did you get tested?

39:35.998 --> 39:37.875
Yes, I got tested for everything.

39:37.958 --> 39:41.045
Goodness, I got this year's
health checkup all cleared.

39:41.712 --> 39:43.839
I have to stay here
until the results come out.

39:44.548 --> 39:46.175
I told your mom about you.

39:46.258 --> 39:48.302
You couldn't wait for half a day?

39:48.386 --> 39:51.222
Hey, no news is good news.

39:51.305 --> 39:52.848
Don't worry, okay?

39:52.932 --> 39:55.434
I told her you're busy
because of the training.

39:56.018 --> 39:58.896
Well, you've got that much sense,
at least.

39:58.979 --> 40:01.649
I'm also looking into this
to find out what's going on.

40:02.483 --> 40:04.026
By the way, where are you?

40:04.110 --> 40:06.570
I don't know.
It looks like a school dormitory.

40:07.488 --> 40:09.657
Hey, don't worry.
I'm sure they won't kill me.

40:09.740 --> 40:12.159
I don't feel particularly ill,
so I can just rest up

40:12.243 --> 40:13.661
until the results are out.

40:13.744 --> 40:17.998
We got the narcotics test results
for our suspect, and he's clean.

40:18.916 --> 40:19.959
Really?

40:21.085 --> 40:22.962
Is it really an infectious disease?

40:23.045 --> 40:24.505
From what I see, it's narcotics.

40:25.589 --> 40:26.966
You really are a cop.

40:27.049 --> 40:28.342
What do you mean?

40:29.260 --> 40:30.803
It's nothing.

40:30.886 --> 40:37.017
Anyway, I'll catch the culprit
and let you rest without any worries,

40:37.101 --> 40:38.644
so just rest there a bit, okay?

40:38.727 --> 40:40.521
Okay, I'll look forward to it.

40:40.604 --> 40:42.148
It's late. Go to bed.

42:47.147 --> 42:49.650
LYTTA VIRUS RESULT REPORT
TEST RESULT: VIRUS NOT FOUND

42:49.733 --> 42:51.402
POSSIBILITY OF FIRST ANTIBODY
NO SYMPTOMS

42:51.485 --> 42:53.821
NO POSSIBILITY OF INFECTION
BUT NEEDS MORE OBSERVATION

43:07.251 --> 43:08.377
YOON SAE-BOM

43:08.460 --> 43:09.628
GRADUATED HIGH SCHOOL 2 YEARS LATE

43:09.712 --> 43:11.589
ENLISTED IN SOU
AFTER DROPPING OUT OF NURSING SCHOOL

43:14.174 --> 43:15.884
ALWAYS EXTREMELY CALM
SMART AND STRONG

43:15.968 --> 43:16.927
EXCESSIVELY CURIOUS

43:29.315 --> 43:31.358
SUPER ROOKIE BASEBALL ACADEMY

43:31.442 --> 43:34.403
Hey, get up. I found it.

43:34.486 --> 43:35.696
What?

43:38.365 --> 43:39.408
You found it?

43:39.491 --> 43:40.576
Let me see.

43:41.243 --> 43:42.244
"Next."

43:44.079 --> 43:44.913
"Next"?

43:46.123 --> 43:47.124
What is that?

43:49.585 --> 43:51.420
Oral medication for pneumonia.

43:51.503 --> 43:53.589
Many antivirus studies
took place during COVID-19.

43:53.672 --> 43:55.090
It came out then,

43:55.174 --> 43:57.926
but the side effects were serious,
so it was quickly dropped.

43:58.010 --> 43:59.053
Side effects?

43:59.845 --> 44:03.641
Addiction, hallucinations, mood swings…

44:03.724 --> 44:05.643
And enhanced concentration too.

44:06.143 --> 44:08.479
It had one good thing about it, at least.

44:08.562 --> 44:10.356
Then why did it pass the drug test?

44:10.439 --> 44:12.941
Causing hallucinations
doesn't just make it a narcotic.

44:13.025 --> 44:15.486
It's a narcotic only when
the law says it's a narcotic.

44:18.322 --> 44:19.365
Hey, Il-ho.

44:20.658 --> 44:21.575
By any chance…

44:22.826 --> 44:28.082
what if this causes something like rabies?

44:28.165 --> 44:31.210
There will be a frenzy.
This has spread widely already.

44:32.586 --> 44:34.421
But that's not going to happen.

44:35.297 --> 44:36.131
Why not?

44:37.508 --> 44:41.136
Nothing has happened until now.
Why would things suddenly go wrong?

44:53.482 --> 44:56.402
SEYANG POLICE STATION

44:57.778 --> 44:59.738
Jung-kook, did you track down that number?

44:59.822 --> 45:02.241
Oh, wait. Here.

45:02.324 --> 45:05.369
They're at a university. Is it a student?

45:06.703 --> 45:08.247
Isn't this a crappy university?

45:08.330 --> 45:10.249
I guess they had terrible grades.

45:12.042 --> 45:12.876
Thanks.

45:12.960 --> 45:13.794
Hey…

45:15.295 --> 45:17.089
Was I too harsh?

45:29.643 --> 45:32.479
No one wakes me up
and I don't have to go to work.

45:32.563 --> 45:33.647
How nice.

45:35.441 --> 45:37.025
It's cold.

45:43.657 --> 45:45.576
Ms. Yoon Sae-bom, please come out.

45:46.285 --> 45:48.620
First Lieutenant, when did you…

45:49.872 --> 45:51.457
Are the test results out?

45:51.540 --> 45:52.916
We're testing you again.

45:56.420 --> 46:01.216
First Lieutenant, please tell me
before you cut my flesh off today.

46:01.300 --> 46:03.135
My feelings will be really hurt.

46:12.144 --> 46:14.480
Are there other patients here, too?

46:21.653 --> 46:22.905
Lee Jong-tae?

46:25.115 --> 46:27.701
- Let me talk to him.
- No.

46:31.121 --> 46:32.331
Ms. Yoon Sae-bom!

46:32.998 --> 46:34.458
Ms. Yoon Sae-bom!

46:36.418 --> 46:37.878
It won't take long.

46:48.138 --> 46:49.723
Are you okay?

46:50.474 --> 46:54.394
I feel a bit cold, but I'm okay.

47:05.447 --> 47:07.699
Do you remember being shot by me?

47:09.159 --> 47:09.993
Yes.

47:10.577 --> 47:13.080
What about biting your fellow trainee
and attacking me?

47:14.081 --> 47:15.874
I don't know.

47:18.126 --> 47:19.044
You do remember.

47:20.879 --> 47:23.632
Ms. Yoon Sae-bom, stand back!
It may be dangerous!

47:23.715 --> 47:26.843
It's okay. He looks fine right now.

47:31.056 --> 47:33.642
Did you go mad after taking a drug?

47:33.725 --> 47:35.310
Where did you get that drug?

47:37.229 --> 47:40.315
I don't know what you're talking about.

47:40.816 --> 47:43.360
The guy you gave
the drug to got arrested already.

47:43.443 --> 47:47.406
You know you'll get an additional penalty
because you're a police officer, right?

47:51.034 --> 47:52.160
Do you see this?

47:53.328 --> 47:55.289
You scratched me, Jong-tae.

47:56.123 --> 47:58.792
They say it's an infectious disease,
but I'm not sure.

47:59.501 --> 48:05.382
We have to find out if it's
a disease or if it's because of the drug.

48:06.550 --> 48:07.968
Understand?

48:09.595 --> 48:12.014
That's the only way
I can be relieved and get tested.

48:16.059 --> 48:17.769
Can I have a drink of water, please?

48:17.853 --> 48:19.062
Absolutely not!

48:19.563 --> 48:20.981
I'm just so thirsty.

48:21.064 --> 48:22.399
She said you can’t.

48:25.861 --> 48:27.195
I'm thirsty.

48:32.159 --> 48:33.702
Hey, what are you doing?

48:34.453 --> 48:36.288
Open your eyes. I'm talking to you.

48:41.918 --> 48:42.878
Hey.

48:57.643 --> 48:58.560
Lee Jong-tae.

49:31.009 --> 49:33.136
Give me water. I'm thirsty.

50:20.225 --> 50:23.520
Lieutenant Colonel Han Tae-seok,
are you there?

50:38.994 --> 50:42.831
THERE ARE NO REDEVELOPMENT PLANS
DO NOT BE FOOLED

50:44.875 --> 50:47.878
You are approaching your destination.

50:55.594 --> 50:57.137
WE OPPOSE REDEVELOPMENT

50:57.220 --> 51:00.849
You have reached your destination.
Ending route guide.

51:07.773 --> 51:09.191
How can we help you?

51:09.274 --> 51:11.485
Isn't this Wonjung University?

51:11.568 --> 51:15.113
It was closed for being substandard
and now the military is using it.

51:16.990 --> 51:19.951
I'm from the police.
Can I meet the person in charge?

51:20.035 --> 51:22.746
This a classified military area,
so I'm afraid you can't.

51:25.457 --> 51:32.422
Then please tell Lieutenant Colonel Han
that I brought the drug I told him about.

51:41.306 --> 51:42.349
Let him in.

51:47.979 --> 51:50.607
You made me meet Lee Jong-tae
on purpose, didn't you?

51:50.690 --> 51:52.317
You even installed a camera there.

51:52.859 --> 51:54.945
I wanted to know when he'd feel thirsty.

51:56.947 --> 51:58.198
Thirsty?

51:58.281 --> 52:00.909
The infected lose their senses
and bite people.

52:00.992 --> 52:02.536
They feel extreme thirst…

52:04.287 --> 52:05.622
but water can't quench it.

52:14.172 --> 52:17.926
They keep feeling thirsty and going crazy
even after coming back to normal.

52:18.009 --> 52:20.554
We're trying to find out
the conditions for that

52:20.637 --> 52:22.222
and I was curious

52:22.305 --> 52:24.683
about how Lee Jong-tae
would react if he saw you.

52:24.766 --> 52:27.811
So you wanted to see how he would be
if he saw the one who shot him?

52:28.562 --> 52:30.397
They can recognize their families,

52:30.480 --> 52:31.940
so I wondered about the others.

52:33.275 --> 52:35.068
That wasn't all of it.

52:36.194 --> 52:39.823
His heart beat slower,
he seemingly felt less pain,

52:40.574 --> 52:42.158
and his wound healed faster too.

52:43.493 --> 52:45.996
If it can be controlled,
it can be lucrative.

52:50.917 --> 52:53.086
So that's why
you're investigating it secretly.

52:53.920 --> 52:57.007
It's not highly contagious,
but it can scare people.

52:57.507 --> 52:59.342
Everyone's already tired of diseases,

52:59.426 --> 53:01.261
so we don't need to make things worse.

53:10.478 --> 53:12.522
So why do you turn
the air conditioners on?

53:12.606 --> 53:15.525
The occurrence of the disease
slows down in low temperatures.

53:21.406 --> 53:23.033
Is this a test too?

53:23.116 --> 53:24.826
To see if I'm thirsty or not?

53:26.369 --> 53:28.663
According to the test results,
you really are okay.

53:30.790 --> 53:33.209
I'm usually not that lucky.

53:34.544 --> 53:36.296
You need to get some rest for a while.

53:37.088 --> 53:38.131
Here?

53:38.882 --> 53:40.634
Wherever you want.

53:42.177 --> 53:45.138
Really? Is that possible?

53:46.348 --> 53:51.061
Just say you contributed to the nation
and got injured in the process.

53:52.062 --> 53:54.356
And we have to collect
your blood every two weeks.

53:55.273 --> 53:57.067
You're not showing any symptoms,

53:57.150 --> 54:00.487
so it means the antibody
might have formed in your body.

54:03.990 --> 54:05.659
THE ARMED FORCES MEDICAL COMMAND

54:10.747 --> 54:13.208
I feel like I'm someone quite important.

54:14.834 --> 54:15.877
One more thing.

54:20.423 --> 54:22.676
I've contributed to the nation.

54:23.843 --> 54:26.596
Then give me
top work evaluation points for this year.

54:27.305 --> 54:28.348
What?

54:28.431 --> 54:31.768
The apartments in Seyang
provided to the police officers.

54:31.851 --> 54:33.520
The selection is based on points.

54:33.603 --> 54:36.856
Newlyweds, family to provide for,
years in service, and work evaluation.

54:36.940 --> 54:38.024
They're all added up.

54:40.193 --> 54:43.113
You're powerful enough
to at least do that, right?

54:45.407 --> 54:47.033
I think that would be possible.

54:47.659 --> 54:49.869
You have a decent evaluation too, so…

54:49.953 --> 54:52.247
I have the best evaluation.

54:52.330 --> 54:54.499
I was born to subdue terrorist attacks.

54:56.918 --> 55:00.171
I'm glad that we're on the same page.

55:03.133 --> 55:06.177
- People don't shake hands these days.
- My phone.

55:11.766 --> 55:14.019
By the way, don't you even offer
breakfast here?

55:22.569 --> 55:25.196
Thank you. I'll enjoy this at home.

55:29.284 --> 55:30.535
Do you have a boyfriend?

55:35.915 --> 55:37.542
It's not that I don't like you,

55:38.376 --> 55:40.670
but the age gap between us is way too big.

55:41.921 --> 55:43.923
Work evaluation points won't be enough.

55:44.007 --> 55:45.508
You'll need more points.

55:45.592 --> 55:47.302
So I was wondering if you had a plan.

55:47.385 --> 55:50.346
I can start making plans now.

55:50.930 --> 55:52.098
Aren't you worried?

55:53.183 --> 55:57.437
I will get the apartment,
so you don't need to worry.

55:57.520 --> 55:59.731
I meant what you saw yesterday and today.

56:00.440 --> 56:04.486
If something goes wrong,
the world may collapse.

56:05.945 --> 56:07.864
Worrying won't change anything.

56:09.532 --> 56:11.117
Perhaps it may not collapse.

56:25.423 --> 56:26.424
First Lieutenant,

56:27.008 --> 56:29.010
what about the clothes I was wearing?

56:30.303 --> 56:31.763
We burned them.

56:34.265 --> 56:35.725
Then should I go home in these?

56:38.770 --> 56:40.855
Yoon Sae-bom? Hey.

56:40.939 --> 56:42.982
Are you okay? Let me see.

56:48.154 --> 56:50.740
First Lieutenant, can't you trust me?

56:51.825 --> 56:53.326
I'm hurt.

56:54.327 --> 56:56.454
They said I'm okay and told me to go home.

56:59.249 --> 57:01.042
I'm sorry. This is because of me.

57:02.627 --> 57:04.712
- You look thinner.
- Really?

57:04.796 --> 57:06.589
It's because I didn't have breakfast.

57:08.091 --> 57:09.425
How did you get in here?

57:10.093 --> 57:14.264
- Did you get caught too? Were you bitten?
- No, I came to rescue you.

57:16.474 --> 57:19.269
Wait here. I need to go talk to someone.

57:28.361 --> 57:29.279
That punk.

57:40.874 --> 57:42.542
I think you're good enough
to play baseball again.

57:48.631 --> 57:51.217
Is this the drug?

57:51.718 --> 57:55.763
Yes, I heard it's
a failed pneumonia medicine.

57:55.847 --> 57:58.349
And I heard that tons of people
have taken that already.

57:58.850 --> 58:01.853
I also heard that wasn't the cause,
but a promise is a promise.

58:03.480 --> 58:05.148
Just because it was okay yesterday

58:06.107 --> 58:08.359
doesn't mean it will be okay today.

58:14.699 --> 58:15.617
Bye.

58:50.235 --> 58:52.070
Come on. I'll take you home.

58:53.488 --> 58:56.658
Yes, it was right next to me.

59:00.745 --> 59:01.621
Yi-hyun.

59:03.373 --> 59:05.583
Do you have a girlfriend?

59:06.167 --> 59:07.293
Why are you asking that?

59:07.377 --> 59:09.003
- Do you?
- I don't.

59:09.087 --> 59:12.048
- Do you snore? Or grind your teeth?
- I don't think so.

59:12.131 --> 59:13.383
Will you marry me?

59:15.343 --> 59:16.177
Jung Yi-hyun!

59:16.803 --> 59:19.806
Tell him that you don't want me
to get punished.

59:19.889 --> 59:21.224
He's going to arrest me.

59:21.307 --> 59:22.642
Hey, Yoon Sae-bom.

59:25.520 --> 59:26.813
Do you want to be my girlfriend?

59:31.943 --> 59:32.819
No.

59:35.238 --> 59:38.533
I told you I was just kidding back then.

59:39.659 --> 59:41.286
I'm not kidding.

59:42.245 --> 59:43.329
I mean it.

01:00:24.120 --> 01:00:26.497
If people suddenly start
to go mad like that…

01:00:27.832 --> 01:00:29.792
Info on Han Tae-seok like you asked…

01:00:31.628 --> 01:00:33.421
I seriously hate him.

01:00:34.047 --> 01:00:35.632
I got a house.

01:00:35.715 --> 01:00:38.301
It won't open.
The lower floors are public rentals,

01:00:38.384 --> 01:00:40.511
and the upper ones are regular apartments.

01:00:41.346 --> 01:00:43.222
I got a call from a journalist.

01:00:43.306 --> 01:00:46.100
There's a way to make money,
and safety is guaranteed.

01:00:46.184 --> 01:00:48.686
- Seung-young!
- We have a problem at the dorm.

01:00:48.770 --> 01:00:51.105
Where are the seriously ill patients?

01:00:51.189 --> 01:00:53.608
But aren’t they living human beings?

01:00:53.691 --> 01:00:55.234
If we're late,
even more people will get hurt.

01:00:57.904 --> 01:01:02.909
Subtitle translation by: Hae-lim Lee
